# Project specific
*.json
!package.json
!tsconfig.json
!.claude/hooks.json
!renovate.json
!.mcp.json
!templates/claude-settings-permissions.json
# Pinned-SHA manifest for the vendored eli5-gate core (#591) - checked in by
# design: it IS the offline gate's source of truth, so the blanket *.json rule
# must not swallow it.
!.claude/eli5-vendor.json
# Declared branch-protection posture (#577, ADR 0004) - checked in by design: it
# IS the posture's source of truth, so the blanket *.json rule must not swallow
# it.
!.claude/branch-protection.json
!templates/playwright-pool.example.json
!templates/sandbox/settings-bash-sandbox.json
# OpenCode provider + agent profile shipped by /cpp:init Tier 7 (issue #752).
# It carries the gemma-implementer permission rules - the mechanical fence for
# the local Gemma lane - so the blanket *.json rule must not swallow it.
!templates/opencode-gemma.json
# Plugin marketplace manifests (issue #477, ADR 0001) - tracked despite *.json
# above. The `**` glob keeps future per-family plugins (Phase B2) covered.
!.claude-plugin/marketplace.json
!plugins/**/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
# Plugin-bundled hook configs (issue #479, Phase B3) - tracked despite *.json.
!plugins/**/hooks/hooks.json
# Negative-control manifests (issue #924) - tracked despite *.json above. A
# control.json IS the executable half of a registration: without it the gate's
# `#: NEGATIVE-CONTROL:` directive resolves to UNRESOLVED and the control never
# runs. The blanket rule already swallowed one silently - `git add` no-ops on an
# ignored path with no error - so the framework shipped with its only control
# inert. The `*` glob covers the next consumer, not just the first.
!controls/*/control.json
# The #953 forced-claim prototype's manifest, claims and anchors (issue #953) -
# same trap, one directory over. Its cases/*/claim.json and cases/*/anchor.log
# ARE the fixture inputs: without them `--selftest` crashes on a fresh checkout,
# and before this line it reported "14/14 cases behaved as registered" against
# files that were not in the repository at all. `git add -A` skipped every one
# and reported success.
# NOT UNCHECKED - checked elsewhere: `forced-claim-check.py --selftest` runs all
# seventeen cases against their registered verdicts and exit codes.
# WHAT WOULD MOVE THIS BACK (issue #936): these negations hold only while that
# directory is prototype fixture data. If it is promoted into controls/ the
# `!controls/*/control.json` line above already covers the manifest and these
# entries should be removed rather than left behind.
# THIS IS THE LESSER HALF OF THE FIX. A negation list is a hand-maintained
# enumeration of places where the blanket rule is wrong, and the line above
# proves how that ages: its own comment says the glob "covers the next
# consumer", and it did not cover this one, because this one is outside
# controls/. Extending the list by one leaves the next location just as
# exposed. The fail-loud half lives in the prototype: --selftest refuses to
# report any result until every input it depends on is tracked by git. That
# covers locations nobody has enumerated yet; this line only covers today's.
!docs/research/forced-claim-prototype-2026-09-15/control.json
!docs/research/forced-claim-prototype-2026-09-15/cases/*/claim.json
node_modules/
.claude/settings*.json
.claude/plans/
.claude/security.yml

# Lease-desk browser sessions (issue #421) - live ledger, pool config, and
# per-session storage-state files are per-workstation state, never tracked.
# (Already covered by *.json above; listed explicitly for intent.)
.claude/playwright-sessions.json
.claude/playwright-pool.json
.claude/playwright-state/

# Grill-me cycle runtime state (issue #426): capture buffer + local learnings
# ledger. Templates/fixtures are tracked; the live per-project files are not.
.claude/friction.jsonl
.claude/friction/
.claude/learnings.md
# md-backend sidecar: per-VM apply/reject ledger (issue #472). Local like
# learnings.md - never shared, never committed.
.claude/learnings.rejected.jsonl

# Legacy/defensive: flow worktrees are now VISIBLE SIBLINGS outside the repo
# (issue #627), so nothing is created here anymore. Kept ignored so any stray
# legacy in-repo checkout (issue #440 native worktrees) is never committed.
.claude/worktrees/

# Deploy-verification baseline (issue #444) - a per-workstation snapshot of
# health + smoke probes captured before a deploy, compared against after.
# Runtime state, like .claude/runs/; never tracked.
.claude/deploy-baseline.json

# Logs
*.log
logs/
# #953 forced-claim prototype anchors (issue #953) - tracked despite *.log
# above. An anchor.log is a fixture INPUT, not output: it is the
# non-claimant-authored record the amendment counter reads, and the
# empty-anchor and anchor-with-noise cases exist precisely to exercise its
# contents. Placed AFTER *.log deliberately - gitignore takes the LAST matching
# rule, so the companion negation for these fixtures' *.json (up beside
# `!controls/*/control.json`) works where it sits only because *.json precedes
# it. The first cut of this line sat there too and was silently inert; a
# two-sided `git check-ignore -v` probe caught it.
# NOT UNCHECKED - checked elsewhere: `forced-claim-check.py --selftest`, which
# refuses to report any case result until these inputs are tracked.
# WHAT WOULD MOVE THIS BACK (issue #936): holds only while that directory is
# prototype fixture data.
!docs/research/forced-claim-prototype-2026-09-15/cases/*/anchor.log

